{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-97720" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the center and radius of the osculating circle to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $P(0,4)$ where $t=1,$ given that $‖{r}^{′}(1)‖=3\\pi ,$ and the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ to the curve is\n\n$$\nT(t)=⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi {t}^{2}}{2}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi {t}^{2}}{2})⟩.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/state.json" "file_sha256" "64f01f78ed8b8e3858aa5b82b7d66b685a5e4d4fa6016946173b7e9aa4c8b6a3"} {"question" "q-97720" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since we are given both the value of $‖{r}^{′}(1)‖$ and the unit tangent $T(t),$ we will use the following formula for the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNotice that $r(1)=⟨0,4⟩,$  since the point $P(0,4)$ is at the tip of $r(1).$ \n\nNow, we find ${T}^{′}(t),$ ${T}^{′}(1)$ and $‖{T}^{′}(1)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi {t}^{2}}{2})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi {t}^{2}}{2}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\pi t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi {t}^{2}}{2}),-\\pi t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi {t}^{2}}{2})⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(1) & =⟨-\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})⟩=⟨0,-\\pi ⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-\\pi )^{2}}=\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the radius of curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(1) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{3\\pi }{\\pi }=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal normal vector at $t=1$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(1) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(1)}{‖{T}^{′}(1)‖}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }⟨0,-\\pi ⟩=⟨0,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the center of the osculating circle is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(1)+R(1)N(1) & =⟨0,4⟩+3⟨0,-1⟩=⟨0,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/state.json" "file_sha256" "64f01f78ed8b8e3858aa5b82b7d66b685a5e4d4fa6016946173b7e9aa4c8b6a3"} {"question" "q-97720" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "322d5ed7379ecde79c17766a7df1325b9e26d769dc0ce036c6a0d7aa3677d918"} {"question" "q-97720" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/state.json" "file_sha256" "64f01f78ed8b8e3858aa5b82b7d66b685a5e4d4fa6016946173b7e9aa4c8b6a3"} {"question" "q-97720" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "The center is $(0,-1)$ and the radius $3$"] ["text" "The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius $3$"] ["text" "The center is $(0,1)$ and the radius $3$"] ["text" "The center is $(0,1)$ and the radius $\\frac{1}{3}$"] ["text" "The center is $(0,\\pi )$ and the radius $\\frac{1}{3}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/state.json" "file_sha256" "64f01f78ed8b8e3858aa5b82b7d66b685a5e4d4fa6016946173b7e9aa4c8b6a3"} {"question" "q-97720" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "The center is $(0,1)$ and the radius $3$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/state.json" "file_sha256" "64f01f78ed8b8e3858aa5b82b7d66b685a5e4d4fa6016946173b7e9aa4c8b6a3"} {"question" "q-132125" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the radius of the osculating circle at the point where $t=0$ for the curve $r(t)=⟨t,\\,{e}^{-t}⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/state.json" "file_sha256" "64f01f78ed8b8e3858aa5b82b7d66b685a5e4d4fa6016946173b7e9aa4c8b6a3"} {"question" "q-132125" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since we are given only the curve $r(t)$, we will use the cross product formula to find the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$, ${r}^{′}(0),$ and $‖{r}^{′}(0)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-{e}^{-t}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(0) & =⟨1,\\,-{e}^{-0}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(0)‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{″}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{e}^{-t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,{e}^{-t}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(0) & =⟨0,\\,{e}^{-0}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross product by considering ${r}^{′}(0)$ and ${r}^{″}(0)$ as $3$-dimensional vectors with zero $z$-components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0) & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\times ⟨0,\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k \\\\  & =k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0)‖ & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of curvature at $t=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(0) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(0){‖}^{3}}{‖{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\sqrt{2})^{3}}{1} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/state.json" "file_sha256" "64f01f78ed8b8e3858aa5b82b7d66b685a5e4d4fa6016946173b7e9aa4c8b6a3"} {"question" "q-132125" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "322d5ed7379ecde79c17766a7df1325b9e26d769dc0ce036c6a0d7aa3677d918"} {"question" "q-132125" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/state.json" "file_sha256" "64f01f78ed8b8e3858aa5b82b7d66b685a5e4d4fa6016946173b7e9aa4c8b6a3"} {"question" "q-132125" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/state.json" "file_sha256" "64f01f78ed8b8e3858aa5b82b7d66b685a5e4d4fa6016946173b7e9aa4c8b6a3"} {"question" "q-132125" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/state.json" "file_sha256" "64f01f78ed8b8e3858aa5b82b7d66b685a5e4d4fa6016946173b7e9aa4c8b6a3"} {"question" "q-132129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the radius of the osculating circle at the point where $t=\\pi $ for the curve $r(t)=⟨{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/state.json" "file_sha256" "64f01f78ed8b8e3858aa5b82b7d66b685a5e4d4fa6016946173b7e9aa4c8b6a3"} {"question" "q-132129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since we are given only the curve $r(t)$, we will use the cross product formula to find the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$, ${r}^{′}(\\pi ),$ and $‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & ={e}^{-t}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(\\pi ) & ={e}^{-\\pi }⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ⟩ \\\\  & ={e}^{-\\pi }⟨1,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖ & ={e}^{-\\pi }\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & ={e}^{-\\pi }\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{″}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-2{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & =2{e}^{-t}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(\\pi ) & =2{e}^{-\\pi }⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ⟩ \\\\  & =2{e}^{-\\pi }⟨0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross product by considering ${r}^{′}(\\pi )$ and ${r}^{″}(\\pi )$ as $3$-dimensional vectors with zero $z$-components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\pi )\\times {r}^{″}(\\pi ) & ={e}^{-\\pi }⟨1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\times 2{e}^{-\\pi }⟨0,\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =2{e}^{-2\\pi }\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =2{e}^{-2\\pi }\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k \\\\  & =2{e}^{-2\\pi }k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )\\times {r}^{″}(\\pi )‖ & =2{e}^{-2\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of curvature at $t=\\pi $ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(\\pi ) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(\\pi ){‖}^{3}}{‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )\\times {r}^{″}(\\pi )‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{({e}^{-\\pi }\\sqrt{2})^{3}}{2{e}^{-2\\pi }} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}{e}^{-3\\pi }}{2{e}^{-2\\pi }} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{e}^{-\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/state.json" "file_sha256" "64f01f78ed8b8e3858aa5b82b7d66b685a5e4d4fa6016946173b7e9aa4c8b6a3"} {"question" "q-132129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "322d5ed7379ecde79c17766a7df1325b9e26d769dc0ce036c6a0d7aa3677d918"} {"question" "q-132129" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/state.json" "file_sha256" "64f01f78ed8b8e3858aa5b82b7d66b685a5e4d4fa6016946173b7e9aa4c8b6a3"} {"question" "q-132129" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{e}^{\\pi }"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}{e}^{\\pi }}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{-\\pi }}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{\\pi }}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}{e}^{-\\pi }"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/state.json" "file_sha256" "64f01f78ed8b8e3858aa5b82b7d66b685a5e4d4fa6016946173b7e9aa4c8b6a3"} {"question" "q-132129" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{2}{e}^{-\\pi }"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/state.json" "file_sha256" "64f01f78ed8b8e3858aa5b82b7d66b685a5e4d4fa6016946173b7e9aa4c8b6a3"} {"question" "q-132194" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the center and radius of the osculating circle to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $P(1,-1)$ where $t=1,$ given that $‖{r}^{′}(1)‖=\\sqrt{13},$ and the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ to the curve is\n\n$$\nT(t)=⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4}},\\,-\\frac{3t}{\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4}}⟩.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/state.json" "file_sha256" "64f01f78ed8b8e3858aa5b82b7d66b685a5e4d4fa6016946173b7e9aa4c8b6a3"} {"question" "q-132194" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since we are given both the value of $‖{r}^{′}(1)‖$ and the unit tangent $T(t)$, we will use the following formula for the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNotice that $r(1)=⟨1,-1⟩,$ since the point $P(1,-1)$ is at the tip of $r(1).$ \n\nNow, we find ${T}^{′}(t)$, ${T}^{′}(1)$ and $‖{T}^{′}(1)‖$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4}}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{3t}{\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4}})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{18t}{\\sqrt{{(9{t}^{2}+4)}^{3}}},\\,-\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{{(9{t}^{2}+4)}^{3}}}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{{(9{t}^{2}+4)}^{3}}}⟨-3t,\\,-2⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(1) & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{{(9({1}^{2})+4)}^{3}}}⟨-3(1),-2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{13\\sqrt{13}}⟨-3,-2⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\frac{6}{13\\sqrt{13}}\\cdot \\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{13\\sqrt{13}}\\cdot \\sqrt{13} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the radius of curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(1) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(1)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(1)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{(\\frac{6}{13})} \\\\  & =\\frac{13\\sqrt{13}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal normal vector at $t=1$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(1) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(1)}{‖{T}^{′}(1)‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}⟨-3,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the center of the osculating circle is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(1)+R(1)N(1) & =⟨1,-1⟩+\\frac{13\\sqrt{13}}{6}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}⟨-3,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-1⟩+\\frac{13}{6}⟨-3,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-1⟩+⟨-\\frac{13}{2},-\\frac{13}{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{11}{2},-\\frac{16}{3}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/state.json" "file_sha256" "64f01f78ed8b8e3858aa5b82b7d66b685a5e4d4fa6016946173b7e9aa4c8b6a3"} {"question" "q-132194" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "322d5ed7379ecde79c17766a7df1325b9e26d769dc0ce036c6a0d7aa3677d918"} {"question" "q-132194" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/state.json" "file_sha256" "64f01f78ed8b8e3858aa5b82b7d66b685a5e4d4fa6016946173b7e9aa4c8b6a3"} {"question" "q-132194" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "The center is $⟨-\\frac{11}{2},-\\frac{16}{3}⟩$ and the radius is $\\frac{13\\sqrt{13}}{6}$"] ["text" "The center is $⟨-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{7}{3}⟩$ and the radius is $\\frac{13}{6}$"] ["text" "The center is $⟨-\\frac{7}{2},\\frac{11}{3}⟩$ and the radius is $\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{3}$"] ["text" "The center is $⟨\\frac{13}{2},-\\frac{16}{3}⟩$ and the radius is $\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{3}$"] ["text" "The center is $⟨\\frac{15}{2},-\\frac{11}{3}⟩$ and the radius is $\\frac{13\\sqrt{13}}{6}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/state.json" "file_sha256" "64f01f78ed8b8e3858aa5b82b7d66b685a5e4d4fa6016946173b7e9aa4c8b6a3"} {"question" "q-132194" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "The center is $⟨-\\frac{11}{2},-\\frac{16}{3}⟩$ and the radius is $\\frac{13\\sqrt{13}}{6}$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/state.json" "file_sha256" "64f01f78ed8b8e3858aa5b82b7d66b685a5e4d4fa6016946173b7e9aa4c8b6a3"} {"question" "q-132201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the center and radius of the osculating circle to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $P(0,1)$ where $t=0,$ given that $‖{r}^{′}(0)‖=\\sqrt{2},$ and the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ to the curve is\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/state.json" "file_sha256" "64f01f78ed8b8e3858aa5b82b7d66b685a5e4d4fa6016946173b7e9aa4c8b6a3"} {"question" "q-132201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since we are given both the value of $‖{r}^{′}(0)‖$ and the unit tangent $T(t)$, we will use the following formula for the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNotice that $r(0)=⟨0,1⟩,$ since the point $P(0,1)$ is at the tip of $r(0).$ \n\nNow, we find ${T}^{′}(t)$, ${T}^{′}(0)$ and $‖{T}^{′}(0)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(0) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0,\\operatorname{sin}⁡0-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨-1,-1⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(0)‖ & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the radius of curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(0) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(0)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(0)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal normal vector at $t=0$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(0) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(0)}{‖{T}^{′}(0)‖}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨-1,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the center of the osculating circle is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0)+R(0)N(0) & =⟨0,1⟩+\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨-1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,1⟩+⟨-1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/state.json" "file_sha256" "64f01f78ed8b8e3858aa5b82b7d66b685a5e4d4fa6016946173b7e9aa4c8b6a3"} {"question" "q-132201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "322d5ed7379ecde79c17766a7df1325b9e26d769dc0ce036c6a0d7aa3677d918"} {"question" "q-132201" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/state.json" "file_sha256" "64f01f78ed8b8e3858aa5b82b7d66b685a5e4d4fa6016946173b7e9aa4c8b6a3"} {"question" "q-132201" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "The center is $⟨-1,0⟩$ and the radius is $2$"] ["text" "The center is $⟨-1,0⟩$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{2}$"] ["text" "The center is $⟨0,-1⟩$ and the radius is $2$"] ["text" "The center is $⟨0,1⟩$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{2}$"] ["text" "The center is $⟨1,1⟩$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{2}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/state.json" "file_sha256" "64f01f78ed8b8e3858aa5b82b7d66b685a5e4d4fa6016946173b7e9aa4c8b6a3"} {"question" "q-132201" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "The center is $⟨-1,0⟩$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{2}$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071188/state.json" "file_sha256" "64f01f78ed8b8e3858aa5b82b7d66b685a5e4d4fa6016946173b7e9aa4c8b6a3"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2534 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
